She visited the bamboo forest in Kyoto and found it heavily overrun by tourists and photo shoots. (Verbatim: "I went to the bamboo forest in is it in kyoto i went to the bamboo forest and they said like you know um i was reading advices online about visiting and it was like it gets really busy and there's a lot of people taking pictures and whatnot so they recommend going super early so i went stupidly early like stupidly early")
She found that even visiting early in the morning did not provide peace, as she encountered large groups with full crews. (Verbatim: "i felt like i spent most i wanted to like just get a nice plain picture of just like the bamboo forest but empty it was so hard it was so hard i had to wander around for ages because like everywhere was like nope can't go here photoshoot over here photoshoot over there and i was like photoshoot all over the place")
She experienced a lack of tranquility at the bamboo forest due to noise from a lawnmower being used early in the morning. (Verbatim: "there was a garden nearby and some guy woke up and was like you know what's also great for an early morning or maybe a girl i don't know but they were like let's let's let's get out the lawnmower yeah yeah this is the best best time for for the lawnmower heck yeah i'm gonna i'm gonna bring out the lawnmower and it's gonna go")
