She finds the UK train system unreliable, often delayed, overcrowded, and expensive, with some services frequently cancelled. (Verbatim: "they're not on time they're not on time and they're not there half the time so yeah it's wild it's wild how bad they are like yeah i wish i was exaggerating or joking but my experience has been just no")
She notes that London has a significantly higher cost of living compared to other UK cities, creating an economic bubble. (Verbatim: "london is a very special place because because london london is its own economic bubble okay so if you go into london everything will cost more just naturally everything has a higher price")
She mentions that people often live outside London and commute in to save on living expenses. (Verbatim: "what people do um is to save on the extremely expensive living cost and everything within london is they will live outside of london and then commute into london to work and then and then go back like so i think you get a lot of those")
